{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-six-canonical-knot-operators","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:six-canonical-knot-operators","kind":"proposition","title":"Six canonical knot operators as Reeb-flow trajectories ($S_3$ realisation)","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-reeb-flow-on-color-coords","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-rho-s3-holonomy-exposition","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-vertex-is-exceptional-divisor"],"tags":["knot-operator","reeb-flow","s3-galois","braid-group","garside-element","color-sectors"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.CategoricalReeb.boundary_perm_realises_S3","text":"six-canonical-knot-operators.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:six-canonical-knot-operators\"></a><p><strong>Conditional on <a href=\"#def:q-reeb-flow-on-color-coords\">The <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Reeb flow in color-sector coordinates</a>.</strong>\n<em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{R}_p</code> be the Reeb bundle over the exceptional divisor at brane point <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p</code>. For each of the six elements <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">w \\in S_3</code>, the corresponding braid word <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta_w \\in B_3</code> generates a unique trajectory across <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{R}_p</code>. Its boundary footprint realises <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">w</code> as a Galois permutation of the colour tubes.</em></p>\n<p>The trajectory-by-trajectory construction of the six boundary\npermutations is given in\n<a href=\"#rem:six-canonical-knot-operators-context\" data-at=\"mass-theory/exceptional-divisor-reeb\">the Reeb-bundle trajectory trace</a>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/six-canonical-knot-operators.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"13.11.10","page":"b/prop-six-canonical-knot-operators","qa":{"counts":{"pass":90,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":13,"unknown":0,"stale":74},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Core.SixCanonicalKnotOperators.boundary_perm_realises_S3","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Core/SixCanonicalKnotOperators.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
